  "subtitle": "A colony with a history",
  "summary": "RimWorld is Ludeon Studios' science-fiction colony simulation, released as version 1.0 in October 2018 after a long public-development period. Survivors arrive on a distant planet and must build shelter, obtain food and establish a settlement. The inhabitants bring skills, relationships and personal needs into that work. The chosen AI storyteller organises events around them, producing raids, visitors and other disruptions. Construction and resource management provide the setting for stories that emerge from what individual people experience and how the colony responds.",
  "body": [
    "RimWorld is Ludeon Studios' science-fiction colony simulation, released as version 1.0 in October 2018 after a long public-development period. Survivors arrive on a distant planet and must build shelter, obtain food and establish a settlement. The inhabitants bring skills, relationships and personal needs into that work. The chosen AI storyteller organises events around them, producing raids, visitors and other disruptions. Construction and resource management provide the setting for stories that emerge from what individual people experience and how the colony responds.",
    "A colonist's abilities affect the work they can perform, while injuries, fatigue and mood change how reliably they do it. A good researcher may be poorly suited to negotiations; a wounded leg can slow someone needed for an urgent task. Bedrooms, meals and relationships influence daily life alongside workshops and stores. Improving production therefore involves more than arranging efficient buildings. The people carrying out the plan need treatment, rest and suitable conditions, and disagreements can make an otherwise orderly settlement difficult to manage.",
    "The environment gives each settlement different pressures. A cold region limits the growing season, while other locations bring heat, disease or different resources. Preparing food and shelter creates room to respond when a fire, animal attack or raid interrupts normal work. Caravans allow trade, journeys and contact with other factions beyond the home map. The storyteller's events connect these systems: losing supplies can change a medical decision, which may alter a colonist's relationships and the next problem the group must solve."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "A colony with a history",
    "People before efficiency",
    "Events that change the plan"
  ],
